@startuml C4_Level1_System_Context_Layered
!include <C4/C4_Context>

title System Context Diagram — Commission Calculator (Layered Architecture: SpringBoot + ORM)

' ============================================================
' C4 LEVEL 1: SYSTEM CONTEXT
' ============================================================
' Shows both layered implementations (springboot and orm) as a
' unified system and the actors and external systems they
' interact with.
'
' PURPOSE:
' Answer: "What is the Commission Calculator and who uses it?"
'
' TWO LAYERED IMPLEMENTATIONS:
' The project contains two layered architecture packages that
' share the same commission domain but differ in persistence
' and security:
'
'   springboot — HashMap repos, JWT auth, Thymeleaf web UI
'   orm        — JPA/Hibernate repos, H2 DB, Flyway migrations,
'                caching, permit-all security
'
' Both coexist in the same codebase as educational examples
' of the same business domain implemented at different
' levels of infrastructure maturity.
' ============================================================

Person(salesRep, "Sales Representative", "Creates deals, views commissions,\nfiles disputes")
Person(salesManager, "Sales Manager", "Reviews team deals, approves\ncalculations, resolves disputes,\nmanages users")
Person(financeAdmin, "Finance Admin", "Manages commission plans,\naudits calculations,\nprocesses payouts")
Person(systemAdmin, "System Admin", "Full system access,\nuser management")

System(springbootApp, "Commission Calculator\n(SpringBoot Module)", "REST API + Thymeleaf web UI.\nJWT-secured. In-memory HashMap\nrepositories. Demonstrates\nSpring Boot fundamentals.")

System(ormApp, "Commission Calculator\n(ORM Module)", "REST API with JPA/Hibernate.\nFlyway-managed H2 database.\nSpring Cache. Demonstrates\nORM and data access patterns.")

System_Ext(h2db, "H2 Database", "In-memory relational database\n(used by ORM module only)")
System_Ext(swaggerUI, "Swagger UI", "Interactive API documentation\nand testing interface")
System_Ext(browser, "Web Browser", "Thymeleaf HTML dashboard\n(SpringBoot module only)")

Rel(salesRep, springbootApp, "REST API or web dashboard", "HTTPS + JWT / Form Login")
Rel(salesRep, ormApp, "REST API", "HTTPS")
Rel(salesManager, springbootApp, "REST API or web dashboard", "HTTPS + JWT / Form Login")
Rel(salesManager, ormApp, "REST API", "HTTPS")
Rel(financeAdmin, springbootApp, "REST API", "HTTPS + JWT")
Rel(financeAdmin, ormApp, "REST API", "HTTPS")
Rel(systemAdmin, springbootApp, "User management API", "HTTPS + JWT")

Rel(ormApp, h2db, "Reads/writes domain data", "JDBC / JPA / Hibernate")
Rel(springbootApp, swaggerUI, "Serves OpenAPI spec", "HTTP")
Rel(ormApp, swaggerUI, "Serves OpenAPI spec", "HTTP")
Rel(springbootApp, browser, "Serves HTML pages", "HTTP + Thymeleaf")

' ============================================================
' DIAGRAM NOTES
' ============================================================
' MODULE COMPARISON:
'
' ┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┐
' │ SpringBoot Module     │ ORM Module                         │
' ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
' │ ConcurrentHashMap     │ JPA/Hibernate + H2                 │
' │ JWT + HTTP Basic      │ Permit-all (educational)           │
' │ Thymeleaf web UI      │ REST API only                      │
' │ Bean Validation       │ Flyway migrations                  │
' │ DTO mapper            │ Spring Cache (@Cacheable)          │
' │ Manual UUID gen       │ @EntityGraph, JOIN FETCH            │
' │ 8 controllers         │ 4 controllers                      │
' │ 5 services            │ 4 services                         │
' │ 5 HashMap repos       │ 6 JPA repos + Specifications       │
' └──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘
'
' Both modules share the same User/Deal/Plan/Calculation/Dispute
' domain but the ORM module uses true JPA entities with
' @ManyToOne/@OneToMany foreign key relationships while the
' SpringBoot module uses plain models with String ID references.
' ============================================================

@enduml
